  "summary": "Mario-Christian Meyer is a Swiss-Brazilian physician and advocate for Amazonian conservation and Indigenous cultural heritage. Born in Argentina, he studied medicine and specialized in developmental neuropsychology and child psychiatry, later teaching at the Sorbonne. His UNESCO research on literacy and learning among Indigenous communities brought him to the Amazon, where he became interested in the relationship between culture, language, health, and traditional knowledge.\n\nMeyer’s work focuses on connecting Indigenous expertise in medicinal plants with Western science and green biotechnology. He founded PISAD, a nonprofit promoting sustainable development and cooperation between Indigenous communities and scientists, and has advanced the Herb’Içana project, which aims to transfer plant-based bioproduction technology to Indigenous communities and support their economic autonomy.\n\nHe has received Brazilian ecology awards, been named a Knight of the French Order of Merit, and been made an honorary citizen of Manaus. His publications and public work address biodiversity, traditional medicine, biotechnology, and environmental protection.",
